# ---- secrets: never commit these ------------------------------------------------
.dsh/
.credentials.yaml
*.credentials.yaml
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# ---- the credential-echo incident: keep the rule explicit -----------------------
# protocol/INCIDENT-credential-echo.md records that a credential VALUE once reached a
# session log. Nothing in this repo should ever carry one; this list is a backstop, not
# the control. The control is that no script prints a credential value.

# ---- local model artefacts: large, and not ours to redistribute -----------------
_models/
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.gguf
*.onnx
.venv*/
venv/

# ---- python --------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---- editors / OS --------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- public datasets: fetched by script, hash-pinned, not vendored -------------
# Banking77 is CC-BY-4.0 and may be redistributed with attribution, but vendoring a copy
# creates a second source of truth that silently goes stale. `src/analysis/fetch_data.py`
# downloads it and verifies a SHA256 instead. Set BENCH_VENDOR_DATA=1 to commit it anyway.
data/banking77/*.csv

# ---- scratch -------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
_sidecar.*.log
tmp/
scratch/

# ---- generated print output: rebuild with src/analysis/p96_render_html.py ----
paper/dist/

# ---- the deposited PDFs: 10 MB of regenerable binary, hashed instead ----------
# paper/pdf/README.md records the exact print command and the SHA256 of each
# deposited file, so a regenerated copy can be proven to match without vendoring
# 10 MB. Same reasoning as data/banking77 below: a committed copy is a second
# source of truth that silently goes stale. The checkers ARE tracked, because
# they encode what "print-ready" means and were each debugged against a real
# false report.
paper/pdf/*.pdf
paper/pdf/_page-*.png
paper/pdf/_zenodo-fields.txt

